I will not:
- run judge, or write a judgement or an outcome;
- accept, approve, seat, lock or promote anything; the seats page says only the Director assigns a seat (R03), and import is not approval (R10);
- treat the member receipt as approval (R05: custody only);
- edit the canonical assignment, the seats, or any page to make the answers pass;
- dispatch or acknowledge;
- commit or push to shared Git, or merge into main;
- claim a fresh-model boot or the Prime seat.
Orientation, if it is ever recorded, is not authority. Live observation, kept separate from the commit: the worktree 00.md now points to contents 01.037.md, not R01's 01.036.md; the packet text is the commit's.
